/-!
# Extended local x86-64 integer model

A handwritten local model, written from the Intel SDM, of a 64-bit-mode
user-level integer subset that contains the existing `X86.Instr`/`X86.Insn`
subset. It is not derived from, or proved to correspond with, the Sail, ACL2
or any hardware description.

* `Ext.Syntax`: instructions (`Ext.Instr`), operands (`RM`, `Mem`), sizes,
  condition codes, and the embeddings `ofInstr`/`ofInsn`.
* `Ext.Raw`: the raw prefix/REX/opcode/ModRM/SIB/displacement/immediate
  structure, the length decoder `parseRaw` and its prefix laws.
* `Ext.Encoding`: the canonical encoder and decoder, their round trip,
  canonicity and truncation theorems, agreement with `X86.encode`/
  `X86.Insn.encode`, and the byte-register REX rule.
* `Ext.Decode`: walking a whole byte string with the decoder
  (`decodeLengths`, `decodeAll`), and what a successful walk proves — that the
  bytes are exactly a concatenation of canonical encodings.
* `Ext.Examples`: encodings checked against assembler output.
* `Ext.Flags`: width-generic flags, the sixteen condition codes in
  three-valued logic, and the meaning of every condition after CMP.
* `Ext.Semantics`: `exec`, with data, divide, undefined-condition and trap
  outcomes, register views, little-endian memory access, and agreement with
  `X86.Insn.exec`.
* `Ext.Lemmas`: per-instruction facts for code generation.
* `Ext.Machine`: PC-driven fetch/decode/execute and its agreement with
  `X86.MState.step`.
-/
